A simplified synoptic chart of southern Africa for a day in January (fictional) shows:

- a low of 1002 hPa centred over northern Zambia, with isobars every 2 hPa;
- a high of 1024 hPa over the ocean south-east of South Africa;
- a station at Mutare: circle three-quarters shaded, shaft pointing north-east with one full feather, two dots to the left, temperature 24 °C;
- a station at Bulawayo: circle one-quarter shaded, shaft pointing east with two full feathers, no present-weather symbol, temperature 29 °C.
